# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for `make test-tsan`.
#
# SQLite's WAL index (-shm) is shared by every handle on a database.  Writers
# update it under shm locks (lock bits / OS file locks); readers read the
# header without a lock, compare its two checksummed copies and retry on a
# torn read, with sqlite3OsShmBarrier ordering the accesses.  TSan cannot see
# that as synchronisation and reports a race when two handles open the same
# file at once (test_concurrent, test_stress).  Master reports it too.
race:walIndexRecover
race:walIndexReadHdr
race:walTryBeginRead
